/-!
# The punctured input of Exposé XVIII-A, Lemma 2.2, from the punctured spectrum bound

Let `X` be a Noetherian scheme on which `n` is invertible, `U ⊆ X` an open subscheme, `η` a
maximal point of `X ∖ U` and `s` a geometric point of `X` over `η`. The base change
`U ×_X Spec(𝒪^{sh}_{X,s})` of the open immersion `j : U ⟶ X` to the strict henselization is the
punctured spectrum of `𝒪^{sh}_{X,s}`: every point of `Spec(𝒪^{sh}_{X,s})` maps to a generization
of `η`; the closed point maps to `η ∉ U`; every other point maps into `U`, since `η` is maximal in
`X ∖ U` and only the closed point lies over `η`, the maximal ideal of `𝒪^{sh}_{X,s}` being
generated by that of `𝒪_{X,η}` (Stacks 07QM).

The ring `𝒪^{sh}_{X,s}` is a strictly henselian Noetherian local ring (Stacks 06LJ) of dimension at
most `dim 𝒪_{X,η}` (Stacks 06LK) in which `n` is invertible. By the stalk formula for higher
direct images (Stacks 03Q9) the stalk of `R^m j_* 𝓖` at `s` is `H^m` of the punctured spectrum,
which vanishes for `m ≥ 2 dim 𝒪_{X,η}`: by the bound `2d - 1` of Exposé XVIII-A, Theorem 1.1
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.PuncturedSpectrumVanishingBound`) when `d = dim 𝒪^{sh}_{X,s} ≥ 1`, and
because the punctured spectrum is empty when `d = 0`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.range_strictHenselizationBaseChangeToStrictHenselization_opensι`: the base
  change of `j` has image the punctured spectrum.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.strictHenselizationBaseChangeOpensιIsoPuncturedSpectrum`: the resulting
  isomorphism of schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.puncturedStalkVanishing_of_puncturedSpectrumVanishingBound`: the
  punctured input `PuncturedStalkVanishing n` from `PuncturedSpectrumVanishingBound n`.

## References

* L. Illusie, *Cohomological dimension: first results*, in Travaux de Gabber sur
  l'uniformisation locale et la cohomologie étale des schémas quasi-excellents, Exposé XVIII-A,
  Theorem 1.1 and Lemma 2.2, Astérisque 363–364 (2014)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03Q9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03Q9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07QM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07QM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06LJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06LJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06LK)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

